-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- closed forms over the primes 2, 3, 5
-- chem/electric.cub's closed form takes roots 2^a 3^b; the tetrahedral vertex also has M = 75 = 3·5² at a vertex with
-- an open index, so the radicals here are Π_p p^{e_p/8} over rad-primes, 0 ≤ e_p < 8, linearly independent over the
-- rationals. A candidate root: its value and its exponents over rad-primes; an entry: the exponents and coefficient.
rad-primes : List Nat
rad-primes = cons 2 (cons 3 (cons 5 nil))
